@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] marshall-tests-database-isolation
Ordinary database tests MUST use SQL sandbox ownership. Tests exercising separate
BEAM nodes or committed transactions MUST clean only their own fixture rows and
MUST NOT rely on the parent process's uncommitted sandbox transaction.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] marshall-tests-real-distribution
Distributed admission/authority tests MUST use at least three independently
started Marshall BEAM instances sharing PostgreSQL. The coordinating test node
MUST NOT count as one of those three instances.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] marshall-tests-opt-in-host
Tests requiring Linux host fixtures MUST remain explicitly tagged and excluded
from ordinary tests. Assertions about failure/revocation MUST inspect resulting
state or access, not merely successful request delivery.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] marshall-tests-public-tls-fixtures
Committed TLS keys and certificates MUST remain disposable test fixtures for
loopback transport tests; production configuration MUST NOT select them. Negative
TLS tests MUST retain wrong-authority, plaintext and hostname failure coverage
where the transport claims those guarantees.
